1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:06,180
YAMU!

2
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,658
You're on the move!

4
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,137
Ladies and gentlemen,
duelists of all ages,

5
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:32,260
DiverCorp is proud to present the
KC Grand Championship Tournament!

6
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:38,037
We've assembled an
outstanding lineup of first

7
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,920
-class duelists from around
the world just for you!

8
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,920
One of which will be proud World Champ!

9
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,200
I think we know who that's gonna be.

10
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,620
Wow, can you believe this crowd?

11
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,710
It's huge.

12
00:01:52,793 --> 00:01:57,440
Look, Joey's trying to scare the
competition with his weird chicken dance.

13
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,640
I need some female friends.

14
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,660
Peace and love, baby!

15
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,940
Try acting normal, just this once.

16
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:14,240
And now, make some noise for
our Master of Ceremonies!

17
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:24,526
Mokuba, do they always
have to be so dramatic?

18
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:30,860
So are you people ready
to get your duel on?

19
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,480
I can't hear you.

20
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,200
I said, are you people ready
to see some dueling or what?

21
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:39,910
Good,

22
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,897
because this time can kick off the greatest
duel monsters tournament ever organized.

23
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,020
And before the week is through,

24
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:50,695
we may have a new International
Duel Monsters Champion!

25
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:56,617
So give it up for the current title
holder, Yugi Moto! Yugi! Yugi!

26
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,818
Give a shout out to your fans, Yugi!

27
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,920
Alright, maybe later!

28
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:12,497
So now, direct your
attention to the Kaimotron!

29
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:17,900
Because it's time to kick off our all-star
tournament with the first round matchup!

30
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:24,580
Starting with Block A, the first
competitor to strap on a duelist will be...

31
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,520
Joey Wheeler! Ah, yeah!

32
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:32,352
I just want to say to my adoring
fans, this one's for you!

33
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:35,800
He'll be facing off against
our mystery duelist!

34
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:41,680
A man whose true identity
remains unknown, Epnard Odom!

35
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:49,871
Hey, pal, I don't know who you are, but
when I win, that mask is coming off.

36
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,400
Where do we know him from?

37
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,760
I don't know. I do.

38
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:57,660
Now moving on to Block B.

39
00:03:58,060 --> 00:04:03,580
Up and cover Leon Wilson faces
the good doctor, Richard Dunk!

40
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:07,080
Cool, Leon's in the first duel, too.

41
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,020
Hey, Leon, you go, boy.

42
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:16,380
But before the duels get underway,
there's someone we all want to hear from.

43
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:19,460
So let's try this one more time.

44
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,920
Yugi, come on up here and say a few words.

45
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,350
What?

46
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:28,400
Pharaoh, I need you.

47
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,740
No, you can do this.

48
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:32,450
But...

49
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:34,620
You can't let your fans down.

50
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,549
What am I supposed to say?

51
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:44,180
Hello, Kaivaland!

52
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,120
Uh, Yugi! What?

53
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,020
I meant come up on stage!

54
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:52,240
Oh, no one said there'd
be public speaking!

55
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:53,610
Come on.

56
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,280
It's Kaiba!

57
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,320
Hey Brawl!

58
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,377
Alright, I'm gonna make this brief.

59
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,700
This is not a show.

60
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:30,199
It's the ultimate test of survival,

61
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:33,400
and it will push everyone
involved to their limits.

62
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:38,417
If you came for a friendly game,
then I'd suggest you go home.

63
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:44,640
This is a ruthless battle, and in the end,
only one duelist will remain standing.

64
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:50,060
Now, if everyone's clear, let's move on.

65
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:53,900
From this moment forward,
Kaivaland is a battlefield.

66
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:58,300
So trust no one, and may
the best duelist win!

67
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:04,600
Kaival! Kaival! Kaival! Kaival! Kaival!

68
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,740
That show-off!

69
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,920
He's just lucky he's not dueling!

70
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:14,860
I know one of these pumps is out to ruin
me, and before this tournament's over,

71
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:16,749
I'm going to find out who.

72
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:29,457
Duelists and Spectators, let the first
round of the KC Grand Championship begin!

73
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:33,840
All tournament matches will
be held on Kaivaland grounds,

74
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,737
but only the two remaining
finalists will be

75
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:40,280
invited back to duel right
here in the Kaival Dome!

76
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:44,440
Match 1 will take place on
our Amazon Adventure Trail.

77
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,320
And Match 2 will be held
beneath the Dragon's Lair Flu.

78
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:52,820
Now, competitors, please report
to your designated locations.

79
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:56,740
It's Leon!

80
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,680
The doctor is in.

81
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:09,001
I guess you should have eaten your apple
today, because this doctor is here to stay.

82
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:15,670
Deck.

83
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:22,500
These cards are unsanitary, young man.

84
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,030
Tissue.

85
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:31,460
Ready? Yeah!

86
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:35,269
Draw five cards and
call me in the morning.

87
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,280
It's a doctor thing.

88
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:42,880
This won't hurt a bit.

89
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,160
Let's do it!

90
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,400
Oh, man.

91
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,113
This dude in the mask looks so familiar.

92
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,560
Wait, isn't that our gym teacher?

93
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:00,100
You mean, is that... Uh-huh.

94
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:03,460
Where is this young whippersnapper?

95
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,660
Hey, where is Joey?

96
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,025
Joey, what are you doing here?

97
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:14,120
Hey, there's a two-for-one
sale on weenies.

98
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:15,810
Joey?

99
00:08:15,893 --> 00:08:18,317
You should be on the
Amazon Adventure Trail.

100
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,600
Guess again, pal.

101
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,115
Joey doesn't duel on an empty stomach.

102
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:25,297
I gotta bulk up for my
first match. Wake up!

103
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,860
Your first match has already started.

104
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:32,957
And if you don't get your butt over to
that dueling site in the next ten minutes,

105
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,687
then you'll be disqualified.

106
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,300
You wouldn't. Hold on.

107
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,117
Ten minutes is a piece of cake.

108
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,435
You'll never make it.

109
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:44,300
The Amazon Adventure is a
15-square-mile virtual jungle.

110
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,540
Drop the dogs.

111
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,040
I have no choice.

112
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,240
I'm gonna have to... Wait! Come back!

113
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:53,830
Joey!

114
00:08:53,913 --> 00:08:54,940
What a spaz.

115
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,080
Oh, well. Suit yourself.

116
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,330
All right.

117
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:08,597
According to this map, we
should duck the boat right here.

118
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,657
After that, the quickness
route seems to be...

119
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:11,570
Land ho!

120
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,420
Joey, wait!

121
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,160
Slow down, man!

122
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,320
This jungle is loaded with...

123
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,470
Pitfalls!

124
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,210
You okay?

125
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,580
This place is the pits.

126
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,160
Nice, Crocs. Deal.

127
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:40,000
Now what? Bring left!

128
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,540
You're on their lap, Joey!

129
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,400
Oh, boy, that's probably
gonna leave a mark. Poor guy.

130
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:59,560
Any time you guys want
to jump in and help?

131
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:02,117
Should we tell them
they're only holograms?

132
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,540
And spoil the fun?

133
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,600
How much time do I have?

134
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:08,740
20 seconds.

135
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,880
Be careful, Joey!

136
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,540
Almost there.

137
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,936
If you're not here in 10
seconds, you're disqualified!

138
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:35,140
Six, five, whoa!

139
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,180
I made it.

140
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,660
With five seconds to spare.

141
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,936
Hey, how'd you get here before I did?

142
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,280
I tried to tell you.

143
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:50,285
There's a secret passageway
for special guests.

144
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,000
No, it's not fair.

145
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,120
I fought off giant snakes.

146
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:05,617
at least you made it on time joey wheeler
it looks like the student is finally going

147
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:08,537
to face his former dual instructor i mean

148
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:11,257
it's time to teach you
a lesson kid i don't

149
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:14,137
think so mystery man now let's rock and

150
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:18,577
roll listen guys we know that voice we do

151
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:23,601
i was a dual monster's master while you
were still running around in a dirty diaper,

152
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,590
sonny boy.

153
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:27,080
You don't scare me, shorty.

154
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:31,337
Yugi, that mystery duelist
sounds just like your grandpa.

155
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,960
It is, but why the disguise?

156
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,711
Perhaps I should explain.

157
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,340
Professor Hawkins!

158
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,440
You mean you knew about this all along?

159
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:45,156
I tried to talk him out of
it, but he wouldn't listen.

160
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:49,237
Arthur, I'm joining the
tournament and that's final.

161
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:53,340
I need to get back in the
action and relive my glory days.

162
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:56,800
I was quite the card
shark in my younger years.

163
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,962
Of course, I'll need a disguise.

164
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,620
I don't want anyone going easy on me.

165
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,190
Disguise?

166
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:09,640
I can't believe he actually had us fooled.

167
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,997
I mean, it is a pretty lame disguise.

168
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:14,962
Well, it looks to me like
Joey is still clueless.

169
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,780
Yeah, what else is new?

170
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:20,085
We should probably tell
Joey to go easy on him.

171
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,769
I'm sure he's a bit rusty.

172
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,350
No, Duke.

173
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,640
Gramps is going to be just fine.

174
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:27,840
Well, let's just hope so.

175
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:31,760
Hey, you invited him,
right? Nope. Actually, Mr.

176
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,960
Moto begged to be let in. Huh?

177
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:37,160
But he taught Yugi everything he knows.

178
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,160
And that's good enough for me.

179
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:42,038
I just hope he doesn't hurt himself.

180
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,007
I'm more worried about Joey.

181
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,280
Prepare to be unmasked, old man.

182
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,460
Let's do it!

183
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,660
I'm showing no mercy today.

184
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,300
And I'll start with this.

185
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:04,040
I summon my Swordsman of
Landstar in attack mode.

186
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:09,220
Then I'll place these two cards
face down and end my turn.

187
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:11,540
Interesting choice.

188
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,737
Now watch and learn.

189
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:17,080
I also place two cards face down.

190
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:21,300
Then I'll call my wandering mummy
to the field in attack mode.

191
00:13:25,780 --> 00:13:27,860
How do you like them appers?

192
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,940
Eh, that saying went
out about 50 years ago.

193
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:34,040
And while we're at it,
so did those overalls.

194
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:41,397
And now I'll attack your mummy
with my swordsman of Landstar.

195
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:44,800
Ah, Joey, your monster
is weaker than his, man.

196
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,310
Thanks.

197
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,047
You don't think I know that?

198
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:51,020
I activate Graceful Dice.

199
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:57,991
Now my monster's attack points will
increase depending on the number I roll.

200
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,370
Ah-ha!

201
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,457
I had a hunch you might try that.

202
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:08,760
And that's why I play
this legendary gambler.

203
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,510
No!

204
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,440
What was that?

205
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:20,960
This trap card automatically activates
whenever my opponent rolls a die.

206
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:25,960
So if I roll a higher number than
you, your card is canceled out. What?

207
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:29,830
Four!

208
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,800
Too bad! So what?

209
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:37,240
Joey always has a backup lane.

210
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:42,892
Now, Skulldice will lower your monster's
strength depending on what I roll.

211
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:53,080
The legendary gambler is a continuous
trap guard, which means I also roll again.

212
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:58,050
Fine!

213
00:14:58,780 --> 00:14:59,610
Oh, well.

214
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,740
Read it and weep. No!

215
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:04,097
Looks like we're back where we started.

216
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:07,240
So, Wandering Mummy, attack his swordsman!

217
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,000
I know you, Joey.

218
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,080
Better than you know yourself.

219
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,500
Look, mystery meathead.

220
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,257
You just got lucky, that's all.

221
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:27,097
So I'll switch my little wing guard
to defense mode and end my turn.

222
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:28,540
Go, short stuff.

223
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,794
Joey's getting schooled by his teacher.

224
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:33,040
He sure is.

225
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:34,740
Poor guy.

226
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,020
My move, Sonny.

227
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,340
I reveal my trap card.

228
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,080
Non-aggression area.

229
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:47,300
Of course, in order to activate it, I
need to discard one card from my hand.

230
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:53,000
Sorry, but I've rendered you unable to
summon any monsters in your next turn.

231
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,230
No way.

232
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:56,600
I'm afraid it gets worse, Junior.

233
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:59,217
I play Mirage of Nightmare.

234
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:05,380
This lets me continue to draw until
I'm holding four cards in my hand.

235
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:10,680
It won't be long before your keister
is removed from this tournament.

236
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:17,080
No one can survive the wrath of Grandpa.

237
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,960
I mean, Apnar.

238
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:22,148
So consider yourself
warned, Whippersnapper.

239
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,700
I don't think so, pal.

240
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:28,077
I hope this isn't a bad time.

241
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:32,520
But I should remind you that
my magic card activates now.

242
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:37,080
This lets me draw three cards,
giving me a total of four in my hand.

243
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:40,140
I know how your magic card works, Zapnog.

244
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:43,780
It also means you have to throw
out three cards next turn.

245
00:16:44,060 --> 00:16:45,320
Or do I?

246
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,670
Ta-da!

247
00:16:46,753 --> 00:16:48,640
Preveal emergency provisions!

248
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:51,497
This allows me to send one magic or trap

249
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:54,286
card on my side of the
field to the graveyard.

250
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:57,517
Oh, and I gain 1,000 extra
life points for good measure.

251
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,517
Why, I oughta...

252
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,617
And of course the card I'm removing is...

253
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:03,980
Mirage of Nightmare!

254
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:09,280
Not only do I get to keep my hand,
but I get some bonus points to boot.

255
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:12,775
Ah, so you want to play rough, do you?

256
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,095
Well, wait till you see what I've got!

257
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,560
How quickly we forget.

258
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,697
My trap card is still in effect,

259
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:27,200
so I'm afraid you can't summon
a monster, my adolescent friend.

260
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,797
You don't have to remind
me how to play the game.

261
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,710
Just go.

262
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:32,660
Apparently I do, Joseph.

263
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:39,380
Now I play a magic card
known as Ancient City.

264
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:52,020
What is that thing?

265
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,997
Well, as the card's name
suggests, it's an ancient city.

266
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:58,597
But that's just the beginning
of my archaeological

267
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:03,160
assault Next I sacrifice wandering mummy

268
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:07,720
In order to summon my ancient giant

269
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:15,937
Of course it comes with a slight
catch As long as it remains face up on

270
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:20,680
the field I have no choice but to attack
you with it And if I don't attack,

271
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:23,380
then I lose 300 of my life points

272
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:27,380
Joey doesn't stand a
chance against that thing.

273
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:31,120
Next, I'll activate a magic
card known as Ancient Key.

274
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:41,160
This key lets me unlock the
power of my stone giant tokens.

275
00:18:50,140 --> 00:18:52,337
And they come with a twist also.

276
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:55,540
So, if I leave them both
face up and don't attack,

277
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:58,980
then 1,000 of my life
points get taken away.

278
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:04,540
Now, ancient giant, attack
his little wing guard.

279
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,240
That's not all.

280
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:15,080
Next, my stone giants will
attack your life points directly.

281
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:31,177
you'll be happy to know that I'm
done for now so I'll place one card

282
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:37,537
face down and end my turn not too
shabby huh one more direct attack

283
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:41,797
and your life points go down to
zilch I'd suggest you come up with

284
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:46,160
a strategy pretty quickly or I'm
afraid your tournament days are

285
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:48,500
Oh, no!

286
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:52,160
You're no match for an old pro like me.

287
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,500
We'll see.

288
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:57,160
With no monsters to
protect you from my giants,

289
00:19:57,520 --> 00:20:00,420
you won't make it past the next turn!
